      "year": "1982",
      "notes": "Excerpts for the apparatus of v1.4, from a document built from the Latin text of aquinas.cc and collated with a scan of Leonine t. 23: the text is the edition's, in modern spelling, and each segment is a printed line with its page, column and line. Words the Leonine editors supplied, and a gap they mark, are between ⟨ ⟩. A paragraph's apparatus gives, at its place, aquinas.cc's reading where the edition reads otherwise in substance (variant), a reference aquinas.cc has in the sentence and the edition has not (reference), and a correction proposed by this document's editor where the text keeps a slip of the edition or a gap it marks (correction). An articulus's apparatus gives text of aquinas.cc that the edition does not print: at q. 9 a. 2 the edition prints \"5. deest.\", so the number 5 is unused and the argument after the fourth is the sixth."
    }
